From 42f511e4c9190a0c31b4314c055207a828246a41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 22:25:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] oplus: vintf: declare the FIDO CA HALs in the device
 framework matrix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The FIDO CA chain ships two AIDL HAL instances in the device (odm) VINTF
manifest (vendor.oplus.hardware.fido.fidoca / fido2ca IFidoDaemon/default,
from manifest_oplus_fido.xml / manifest_oplus_fido2.xml). This build
enforces VINTF compatibility (checkvintf --check-compat, FCM >= 202504),
which requires every device-manifest HAL instance to be specified in a
framework compatibility matrix, otherwise:

  ERROR: files are incompatible: The following instances are in the device
  manifest but not specified in framework compatibility matrix:
      vendor.oplus.hardware.fido.fido2ca.IFidoDaemon/default (@1)
      vendor.oplus.hardware.fido.fidoca.IFidoDaemon/default (@1)

Declare both as optional device HALs in device_framework_matrix.xml
(DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE), mirroring the existing
cryptoeng / fingerprintpay / camera.aon entries. Placed next to the other
biometrics HAL. Clears the check_vintf_compatible failure.

(cherry picked from commit f08265c1c03cc7d485cd1de2a0ed528c2a6497c9)

Ledger: hardware_oplus.md Accepted Group C row 13 (f08265c1)
Stub-matrix: task-9-stub-inventory.md row K14 — consumer: framework matrix must match shipped vendor FIDO/keystore CA HALs (build-dep/vintf, attestation lane); location: vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml
Change-Id: I78d329b96d74ee205ea6af82079ed22e5852dcfc
---
 vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml b/vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml
index eb51b304..bcbcd568 100644
--- a/vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml
+++ b/vintf/device_framework_matrix.xml
@@ -33,6 +33,22 @@
             <instance>default</instance>
         </interface>
     </hal>
+    <hal format="aidl" optional="true">
+        <name>vendor.oplus.hardware.fido.fidoca</name>
+        <version>1</version>
+        <interface>
+            <name>IFidoDaemon</name>
+            <instance>default</instance>
+        </interface>
+    </hal>
+    <hal format="aidl" optional="true">
+        <name>vendor.oplus.hardware.fido.fido2ca</name>
+        <version>1</version>
+        <interface>
+            <name>IFidoDaemon</name>
+            <instance>default</instance>
+        </interface>
+    </hal>
     <hal format="aidl" optional="true">
         <name>vendor.oplus.hardware.camera.aon</name>
         <version>1</version>
-- 
